## Re-bootstrapping

When a project already has a `.bootstrap` file, this is a **re-bootstrap** — the project was previously set up with this skill and needs to be brought in line with the current version.

### Flow

1. Diff `.bootstrap-skill` against `~/.claude/skills/python-bootstrap/SKILL.md`
2. Summarize the changes to the user before making any modifications
3. Walk the checklist (see bottom of this file), focusing on areas affected by the diff
4. Apply changes, then update `.bootstrap` (date) and `.bootstrap-skill` (full copy of current SKILL.md)

### What counts as a re-bootstrap

- User says "bootstrap", "modernize", or "update tooling" on a project that has `.bootstrap`
- If `.bootstrap` exists but `.bootstrap-skill` is missing, treat it as a full re-bootstrap (walk entire checklist)

