## New Project Quick Start

```bash
mkdir myproject && cd myproject
uv init --package myproject
# Rearrange into src/ layout if uv didn't already
uv add --group dev ruff pyright vulture pytest pytest-asyncio pytest-cov pytest-xdist pytest-timeout pytest-testmon
# Replace pyproject.toml contents with the template in core-templates.md
# Create the justfile from the template in core-templates.md
# Create .gitignore from the template in core-templates.md
# Create typings/ and vulture_whitelist.py
mkdir -p typings
touch vulture_whitelist.py
uv sync --group dev
git init && git add -A && git commit -m "Initial project setup"
dcat init    # initialize issue tracking
# Write CLAUDE.md — see template below
# If CLAUDE.md already exists, incorporate the dcat section into it
# Write .bootstrap and .bootstrap-skill (see Bootstrap Stamp below)
```

### Project Layout

```
myproject/
  src/myproject/
    __init__.py
    app.py
  tests/
    conftest.py
    test_app.py
  typings/               # stub files for untyped third-party deps
  pyproject.toml         # ALL config lives here — single source of truth
  justfile               # task runner
  uv.lock                # committed to git
  vulture_whitelist.py   # dead code whitelist
  .dogcats/              # dcat issue tracking (committed to git)
  CLAUDE.md              # agent instructions (dcat workflow + project-specific)
  .python-version        # pin python version (created by uv)
  .gitignore             # see template in core-templates.md
  .bootstrap             # skill name + date of last bootstrap
  .bootstrap-skill       # full snapshot of SKILL.md at last bootstrap
  Dockerfile             # optional — multi-stage uv build
```

